    <!-- T20b (PLAN_V0145): one-time system-level network-revoke invite after the
         download. The app never touches the network by itself afterwards. -->
    <string name="setup_net_invite_title">Revoke network permission</string>
    <string name="setup_net_invite_body">The model download is complete — the app no longer accesses the network on its own. If you want, you can revoke the app’s network permission here in the Android system settings; the keyboard keeps working fully offline.</string>
    <string name="setup_net_invite_button">Revoke network permission</string>
    <string name="setup_net_invite_later">Later</string>

    <string name="setup_privacy_text">Your speech and your text stay on this device. The app uses the network exclusively for the one-time download of the speech recognition model (approx. 671 MB) from the specified address; there is no telemetry, no accounts and no cloud recognition. After that download the app no longer accesses the network on its own. You can revoke the app’s network permission entirely in the Android system settings — the keyboard keeps working unchanged, offline. Without an installed model the keyboard stays usable, the voice feature is disabled.</string>

